  "premises": [
    "The device model of 2026-10-04: IEEE32 binary32 results with the canonical NaN, race-free dispatch, the host's length word, a dispatch that covers the count, and no dynamic errors",
    "A loop whose condition still holds at its 2^64-th test has no result in the model; Dawn and naga end a loop at that test",
    "One buffer per IR parameter: an array's Wasm array, or a scalar's two words, with arrays and the count below 2^29 elements"
  ],
  "result": "The dispatch leaves the output holding the Lean function's build as a Wasm array, distinct invocations store to distinct words, and the printed text parses to the kernel; the Wasm theorem of the same function follows from the same element lemma.",
